# SPA routes → the app shell, status 200 (link previews and crawlers need 200).
# Rewrite to "/", never "/index.html": Pages strips index.html, so a
# "/* /index.html 200" rule is dropped as an infinite loop.
# No catch-all: _redirects beats static files, so "/*" would serve HTML
# for /assets/*.js. Unknown paths fall to the app shell (404.html, which is
# a copy of index.html). MEASURED 2026-10-20: the shell answers an unknown
# path with status 200 when the copy is in the build, and with status 404
# when it is not — so both build paths make the copy and one commit always
# behaves the same way.
